course: dictionary
lesson: 10546
title: Small word, big meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «un» is tiny, but it does a lot of jobs. At the start of an English word, «un-» means «not» or «the opposite of». «Unhappy» means not happy, «unkind» means not kind, and «unlock» means do the opposite of lock.
explain: Capital letters change the meaning. «UN» stands for the United Nations, a group of nearly all the countries in the world that works for peace. On the news you might hear, «the UN's top court», which is a court that works for the whole UN.
explain: «Un» is also a French and Spanish word meaning «a» or «one». So «un temps de chien» means «a dog's weather», a very bad, stormy day. Even in English, speakers sometimes clip «one» to «'un», as in «a good 'un», meaning a good person.
fact: The prefix «un-» at the start of a word usually means «not» or «the opposite of».
fact: «Unknown» means not known, and in maths it can be the number we are looking for.
fact: «UN» in capital letters means the United Nations, which works for peace between countries.
fact: In French, «un» means «a» or «one», as in «un temps de chien», «a dog's weather».
fact: Quatre-vingt-un has no s and no et, because the s on «quatre-vingts» is only used when no other number follows it.
exercise: In «unkind», what does un- mean? | *not, the opposite of, as in unkind meaning not kind | very | not | again
exercise: In «the UN's top court», what does UN stand for? | *United Nations | United Namibia | Universal News | Under Nine
exercise: In French «un temps de chien», what does «un» mean? | *a | with | not | the
test: Which word means «not happy»? | happen | hap | *unhappy | happily
test: Which word completes this French number: 81 is quatre-vingt-___? | dix | et un | *un | uns
exam: In UK speech, what does «a good 'un» mean? | a good dog | a good meal | *a good person | a good number
